Build fix: explicitly include <linux/hex.h> for hex2bin().

Kernel 7.0 finishes cleaning up <linux/kernel.h> and no longer pulls in
the hex2bin() prototype transitively. The driver calls hex2bin() in
rtl8152_get_mac_pass() (r8152.c:2192) but relies on an indirect include,
which breaks with:

    r8152.c:2192:8: error: call to undeclared function 'hex2bin';
    ISO C99 and later do not support implicit function declarations

Add the explicit include, guarded by __has_include so older kernels that
do not ship <linux/hex.h> as a standalone header keep working — in those
kernels hex2bin() is still reachable via <linux/kernel.h>.

--- a/r8152.c	2025-11-28 17:15:54.000000000 +0200
+++ b/r8152.c	2026-04-19 12:00:00.000000000 +0300
@@ -30,6 +30,9 @@
 #include <linux/suspend.h>
 #include <linux/atomic.h>
 #include <linux/acpi.h>
+#if __has_include(<linux/hex.h>)
+#include <linux/hex.h>
+#endif
 #include "compatibility.h"

 #if LINUX_VERSION_CODE >= KERNEL_VERSION(6,4,10)
